   "title": "Troubleshooting Database Query Timeouts and High Replication Lag in Metrics Engine",
   "content_summary": "Guidance for resolving query timeouts, replication lag, and disk usage alerts in Metrics Engine caused by resource exhaustion or capacity limits.",
   "content_body": "When Metrics Engine reports high replication lag or query timeouts, first check if disk usage has crossed critical thresholds or if the database is out of disk space. These symptoms often stem from resource exhaustion or underlying capacity limitations that prevent index rebuilds from completing successfully. Verify the status of recent backup jobs, as failed backups can contribute to data quality issues or locked resources. The typical resolution involves executing a capacity increase for storage or compute resources, followed by running a data repair script if index corruption is detected. If manual reconciliation of replication states is required due to prolonged lag, adjust rate limits to stabilize the ingestion pipeline during recovery."
